{
  "requirement": "Every {term}`requirements.sdk.graph.validation.criterion` type implements\n`trust_but_verify::graph::Criterion<D>` for its\n{term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain`:\n\n```rust,ignore\n// Defined in trust_but_verify::graph.\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligation.** Every criterion type implements `trust_but_verify::graph::Criterion<D>` for its application domain. The trait is `pub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized`. The testable parts are:\n- Criterion types, both test-defined and the production one, implement the trait for a concrete `Domain`.\n- Those types can be used through the trait.\n- The `Send` supertrait is honored.\n- `Sized` is honored, which holds automatically for any value type.\n\n**Coverage.**\n- Test-defined criterion types implement `Criterion<D>` and run through `Validator::verify`, `store_evidence`, `load_evidence` and `check_inputs`. They are `Review` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs` (`Criterion<Memory>`), `Review<O>` in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs` (`Criterion<Application>`), and `Review` in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs` (`Criterion<Memory>`).\n  - The tests are `deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent`, `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested`, and `caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly`.\n  - They assert on the resulting outputs, source node, path, revision, dependencies, and the execution and write counts. A type that lacked a conforming implementation would not compile or would fail these assertions.\n- The production criterion `Review` in `src/authoring/sdk.rs`, which implements `Criterion<ReviewGraph<'_>>`, is tested by `review_graph_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk`. That test calls the criterion's `source_node_id`, `criterion_path` and `revision`, then runs `verify`, `store_evidence`, `load_evidence` and `check_inputs` through the trait with a real domain.\n- The `Send` bound is exercised by `validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync`. Its `Review<Cell<_>>` criterion holds a `Cell` and is therefore `Send` but not `Sync`. The test wraps `verify`, `store_evidence`, `load_evidence` and `refresh_evidence` in `send(..)`, whose bound is `T: Send`, so it fails to compile if the criterion or its futures are not `Send`. This shows that the trait demands `Send` and not `Sync`, and that a `Send`-only type still implements the trait. `Sized` is exercised implicitly, because every criterion is used by value.\n\n**Gaps.** I found none.\n- The sub-requirements (`answer`, `source_node_id`, `revision`) are separate requirements and are tested under their own references.\n- The tests contain no compile-fail test for a `!Send` criterion. The `send(..)` wrapper on futures that carry the criterion value already ties the future's `Send`-ness to the criterion's, so removing the supertrait would break compilation. Such a test is not needed.",
  "references": "705f083029c396c6545af7e6b8e263effa08721adff8c3cf33a5fab57044d3ac",
